Description:
    Writes config/search.yml and config/search.rb.

    config/search.yml says which store each environment searches through.
    config/search.rb is where each index is declared. Neither file is
    overwritten if it is already there.

    --adapter says what development and test search through. It defaults to
    sqlite, which needs no connection details because a database adapter takes
    them from the document class. Every other adapter defaults to localhost on
    its own port, so a local instance needs no connection details either. It
    may still need the index itself: a Solr core, for one. Typesense is the
    exception and has no default key, so set TYPESENSE_API_KEY.

Example:
    bin/rails active_search:install
    bin/rails active_search:install ADAPTER=elasticsearch

    creates: config/search.yml
    creates: config/search.rb
